Parameter Type Default What it does <code>page</code> integer ≥ 0 <code>0</code> Page, starting at zero. <code>size</code> integer 1–50 <code>20</code> Rows per page. <code>webtracking_summary</code> defaults to <code>50</code>. <p>The response includes:</p> <pre><code>{
  "pagination": {
    "total": 3252,
    "page": 0,
    "size": 20,
    "totalPages": 163,
    "nextPage": 1
  }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>nextPage</code> is <code>null</code> on the last page. <code>Maximum rows per tool call</code> reduces <code>size</code> below the maximum of 50 allowed by the schema.</p>

Parameter Type What it does <code>sortField</code> string Sort field. Each tool publishes its list. <code>sortDirection</code> <code>ascending</code> or <code>descending</code> Sort direction. <code>sortMultipleFields</code> object Up to three fields with their direction. Cannot be combined with <code>sortField</code>/<code>sortDirection</code>. <p>Example:</p> <pre><code>{
  "sortMultipleFields": {
    "priority": "descending",
    "startDate": "ascending"
  }
}
</code></pre>
